From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:10:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: orangepi-zero: add mmc aliases

The MMC core numbers hosts after the "mmcN" aliases and falls back to
probe order when a host has none. The Orange Pi Zero2/Zero3 DT only
declares ethernet0/serial0, so the microSD slot (mmc0) and the SDIO
WiFi module (mmc1) race: depending on which host probes first the SD
card shows up as /dev/mmcblk0 or /dev/mmcblk1 (observed on a Zero2
across reboots). Root is mounted by UUID so boot survives, but tools
and documentation referring to /dev/mmcblk0 hit the wrong or a missing
device.

Pin the numbering with aliases, as other H616/H618 boards (Tanix TX6s,
Mellow Fly C5, WalnutPi) already do: mmc0 = SD, mmc1 = SDIO WiFi. mmc2
(eMMC) is not wired on either board.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero.dtsi
@@ -15,6 +15,8 @@
 / {
 	aliases {
 		ethernet0 = &emac0;
+		mmc0 = &mmc0; /* microSD slot */
+		mmc1 = &mmc1; /* SDIO WiFi/BT module */
 		serial0 = &uart0;
 	};
 
